CI evidence and decisions

Run 32489660482 exposed two portability gaps under environments not available in the original local pass.

Rust 1.98 strict Clippy reported chunks_exact_to_as_chunks in the CEF nonce verifier and Ollama SHA parser, plus result_large_err at the SearXNG async publication boundary. The conversions use fixed-size as_chunks after the existing length checks. The nonce comparison still accumulates every XOR word before deciding. Rejected SearXNG handles are boxed only at the uncommon ownership-return boundary so cleanup retains the exact child handle without inflating every async result.

The Windows tests compiled Unix process_tree code because its module used cfg(any(unix, test)), and two platform-neutral receipt tests depended on a Unix-only fixture. The Unix implementation and imports are now cfg(unix); the neutral tests use a plain temporary directory. No test behavior is disabled on its supported platform.

